  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe column simulation cuts cylinder stock along X or Y, in either direction.\nIt uses analytic circle sections for the top and the rounded underside.\nRemoved volume stops at the real underside.\nCarried stock uses the same underside.\nThe viewport draws the laid stock through its existing placed mesh.\nThe grid builder moves to a separate module to keep the simulation facade near 400 lines.\nThe decision is in docs/decisions/2758-laid-cylinder-sim.md.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe grid builder only represented upright cylinders.\nThe frame law refused a horizontal cylinder before simulation.\nA constant initial top and floor cannot measure the material in a laid cylinder.\n\n## Tests\n\n- laid_cylinders_cut_only_their_real_material_along_x_and_y\n- laid_cylinder_refuses_invalid_dimensions_by_name\n- laid_cylinder_padding_and_translation_keep_exact_material_sections\n- the_sim_frame_keeps_square_stock_and_refuses_oblique_stock\n- the_eye_draws_the_laid_bars_rotated_stock\n\nThe application pin failed on unchanged upstream/main e048b103c with the named laid-cylinder refusal.\nThe pin passes with the fix.\nEight mutations failed by assertion and passed after restoration.\nThey cover the frame, grid, removal measurement, carry floor, translation, dimensions, end bound and radial bound.\nThe first four mutations restore the original files from upstream/main.\nThe translation mutation removes only the new metadata shifts, because the old file lacks the new struct field.\nThe new analytic module has no old file. Its three guard mutations remove one guard at a time.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 111 steps on the review follow-up.\nIt reported 1,244 passed tests, 0 failed tests, and 20 ignored tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed with exit code 0.\n\n## Heavy lane results\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` ran on head `1e7cb593abc27823e5051e0fa9d5f56dd4de88e3`.\nThe initial heavy run used `upstream/main` at `3970d3d0319e423761c48f9a7e0a6391a14b9403`.\nThe shared ref advanced externally during verification.\nThe retry and quick gate used `c4ac3ce6da5d79e572b82ec94bc965427cd63eeb`.\nRef reflog timestamps confirm these values.\nBoth refs have the same merge base with the PR head: `e048b103ca649e24048268e1a050f0b4686a997a`.\nEach gate plan selected the same 14 changed files.\n\n| Release lane | Passed | Unexpected failures | Ignored |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `motion heavy` | 56 | 0 | 0 |\n| `app heavy` | 42 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThese counts exclude three registered probes for issue #1950.\nThe gate accepted their expected failures: two in motion and one in app.\n\nThe first run completed 217 steps, with 216 green steps.\nThe shared release build failed because the sccache server reset its connection.\nAll heavy tests ran in that run.\nThe retry disabled sccache and ran the failed build step and the three registered probes.\nAll four retry steps passed.\nAll 217 planned steps passed across the first run and the retry.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff of .nc and .cl files is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe live GUI was not exercised.\nOptional oblique stock support is not implemented. The named refusal remains.\nThe development field carry engine still refuses cylinder stock.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2714 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes planning in stock_sim.rs and registers a field module in stock_sim/mod.rs.\nThis PR extracts stock_grid and registers the analytic cylinder module in a different location.\nPR #2773 has no file overlap. Its Stock page note calls sim_frame, so its laid-cylinder note test needs the new expectation.\n\nEffort: max. The issue did not escalate.\n\nChangelog: Stock simulation cuts cylinder stock along X or Y and measures removal against the rounded underside.\n\nFixes #2758\n",
